\" height=\"147\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"3:126\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"229\">\n          <text id=\"3:127\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"197\" height=\"24\" />\n          <text id=\"3:128\" name=\"• Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen • All other colors: neutrals, text, surfaces, gain / loss, risk levels, accents, chart colors • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation • All states: current page, selected tab, pressed, disabled, amount being entered, rising / falling • Headers, page indicator, sheets and all business components • Chart and share-of-assets styling, confetti\" x=\"24\" y=\"58\" width=\"596\" height=\"147\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"3:129\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"64\" y=\"3335\" width=\"1312\" height=\"291\">\n      <text id=\"3:130\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"222\" height=\"36\" />\n      <text id=\"3:131\" name=\"Your file is compared with the brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"52\" width=\"1312\" height=\"23\" />\n      <text id=\"3:132\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Flow &amp; prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (current page, current coin-list tab, gains vs losses, risk levels, amount being entered)\" x=\"0\" y=\"91\" width=\"1312\" height=\"161\" />\n      <text id=\"3:133\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 5 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" x=\"0\" y=\"268\" width=\"1312\" height=\"23\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not 