{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I have:\n\n**01 · Foundations**: Brand primary #2B2D33 (graphite), Nunito font (Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold/ExtraBold). Canvas 375×812 iPhone, light mode. Everything else is mine to define.\n\n**02 · Components**: \n- Button (3:19) symbol 335×52\n- Text Field (3:22) symbol 335×48\n- Status Bar (3:26) 375×44\n- Home Indicator (3:36) 375×34\n\n**04 · Media**:\n- Coin logos (symbols 48×48): Coin_BTC (2:8), Coin_ETH (2:11), Coin_USDT (2:14), Coin_BNB (2:17), Coin_USDC (2:20), Coin_BUSD (2:23), Coin_XRP (2:26), Coin_DOGE (2:29), Coin_ADA (2:32), Coin_MATIC (2:35), Coin_DAI (2:38), Coin_AVAX (2:41), Coin_CAKE (2:44), Coin_MANA (2:47), Coin_MKR (2:50), Coin_NEAR (2:53), Coin_DASH (2:56), Coin_ETC (2:59)\n- Avatar_Neutral (2:65) 40×40\n- Icons: Icon_Send (2:75), Icon_Receive (2:80), Icon_Add (2:85), Icon_Scan (2:95), Icon_Search (2:100), Icon_Face_ID (2:106), Icon_Swap (2:112), Icon_Backspace (2:118), Icon_Back (2:123), Icon_Close (2:128)\n\n**03 · Workspace** (4:2): empty page.\n\nNote: Share of Assets needs MATIC, MANA, CAKE, DOGE, MKR logos — all available. Strategies need BTC/ETH/USDT, MATIC/MANA/CAKE, NEAR/DASH/AVAX, ETC/DAI/BNB — all available. Trending coins need BTC, ETH, USDT, BNB, USDC, BUSD, XRP, DOGE, ADA, MATIC — all available. Wallet assets need ETH, DAI, AVAX, CAKE — all available. \n\nNow I need to see the design details of the given components (Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator) to reuse their styles. Let me use get_design_context on the components frame 1:3 to see details, and maybe a screenshot. Actually, since these are symbols/components, I can clone them into my workspace. The best approach: clone the symbols from 02 · Components and 04 · Media into the workspace (or create instances). Components (symbols) can be instantiated via figma.createComponent... Actually in the Plugin API, I can find the component nodes by ID and call `component.createInstance()`.\n\nLet me first call get_design_context on the components and media to understand colors/fills of Button and Text Field. Actually the note says \"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design\". Let me call get_design_context for node 1:3 (Components) to get the details. That might be large. Let me do it for 1:3 and maybe a portion of 1:4. Actually for media, I'll just clone the symbols directly by ID, so I don't need full details. But I need details for Button and Text Field to know their colors.\n\nAlso I should check the design of Status Bar and Home Indicator.\n\nLet me call get_design_context on 1:3 (components page frame 3:15). That includes Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator.\n\nPlan for building:\n\n1. Read design context of components page.\n2. Write a use_figma script that:\n   - Sets up variables/styles? Simpler: define constants in code.\n   - Load fonts: Nunito Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold, ExtraBold.\n   - Clone needed media symbols into workspace as hidden \"assets\" area? Better: create instances of the components directly. The media symbols are components (symbol = COMPONENT node type in metadata). I can get them via figma.getNodeById and createInstance().\n   \n   Since the file is a copy (writable), the components live in the same file, so instances will work fine.\n\n3. Build 5 frames in 03 · Workspace:\n   - Position them side by side: 01_Wallet at x=0, 02_Discovery at x=475, 03_Strategy at x=950, 04_Invest_Amount at x=1425, 05_Invest_Success at x=1900. With some gap. Actually since 03/04/05 are sheets over 02_Discovery, it'd be good to show them overlapping? No — better to keep them side by side for clarity, each a full 375×812 frame. The \"sheet over 02_Discovery\" presentation means the sheet content sits over a dimmed 02_Discovery background within the frame.\n\n4. Components to create in workspace (as reusable components):\n   - I'll create components for: asset row, pocket card, strategy card, coin row, for-you card, keypad key, tab chip, page indicator, section header, facts chip, share-of-assets row, etc. Given the scale, I'll create a reasonable set of components and use instances.\n\nGiven the complexity and the tool limits (50k chars per call, and it's better to build in manageable sections), I'll structure the build:\n\n**Script 1**: Setup — load fonts, define design tokens (colors), create the 5 frames with backgrounds, status bar, home indicator instances. Also clone media symbols into a hidden \"Assets/Media\" area on the workspace? Actually I can directly instantiate media components by ID — no need to clone.\n\nWait — can I instantiate components from other pages in the same file? Yes, components are file-wide. `figma.getNodeById(\"2:8\").createInstance()` works.\n\nBut careful: the metadata shows `symbol` nodes. Those are COMPONENT nodes in the plugin API. \n\n**Design system decisions** (light mode):\n- Background: #F6F7F9 (light gray) for app background; surfaces white #FFFFFF.\n- Text primary: #2B2D33 (brand graphite doubles as text color).\n- Text secondary: #8A8F98.\n- Gain (positive): #12A354 (green). Loss (negative): #E5484D (red).\n- Accent blue for links/highlights: #3B6EF6? Hmm, brand is graphite. Use graphite for primary buttons; accent for interactive highlights maybe #5B6BF5? Let me keep a restrained palette: primary buttons graphite #2B2D33; accent for selected tab chips: graphite or a blue. I'll use a blue accent #3D7BF7 sparingly? Actually to keep consistency, use graphite as primary interactive color, green/red semantics, and light gray chips.\n\nLet me define tokens:\n- bg: #F2F3F7\n- surface: #FFFFFF\n- ink: #2B2D33\n- ink2: #6B707B (secondary text)\n- ink3: #9AA0AB (tertiary)\n- line: #E8EAEF (hairlines)\n- gain: #16A34A\n- loss: #EF4444\n- chip: #EEF0F4 (light chip bg)\n- brand: #2B2D33\n- overlay: rgba(0,0,0,0.45)\n- sheet radius 24\n- card radius 16\n- Type scale: \n  - Balance: 32 ExtraBold\n  - Section header: 18 Bold\n  - Card title: 15 SemiBold\n  - Body: 13 Medium\n  - Caption: 11 Medium\n  - Micro: 10 Medium\n\nFonts: Nunito styles: \"Regular\", \"Medium\", \"SemiBold\", \"Bold\", \"ExtraBold\".\n\nNote the gotcha in tool description: for Inter it's \"Semi Bold\" — but Nunito in Figma has \"SemiBold\" and \"ExtraBold\" as style names. The Foundations text says \"Regular / Medium / SemiBold / Bold / ExtraBold available\". I'll load with those names, and handle errors by trying alternates.\n\n**Screens**:\n\nCommon: Status Bar component instance (3:26) at top, Home Indicator (3:36) at bottom y=812-34=778.\n\n**01_Wallet** (375×812):\n- Status bar (44)\n- Header: Avatar (40) + \"My Wallet\" + address 0xc8...320f + scan icon (right)\n- Balance block: $54,292.79 (32 ExtraBold), +5.21% (green, maybe chip with arrow)\n- Actions: Send / Receive buttons (two pill buttons with icons)\n- Section \"Assets\" header\n- 4 asset rows: logo 36-40, name, holding (caption), value + 24h change (right, green/red)\n- Section \"Pockets\" header + Add Pocket button?\n- Pocket cards: My New House 🏡 $15,642.40 +7.86%; Tesla Model S Plaid 🚙 $28,389.21 −2.13%; Add Pocket card with + icon.\n- Bottom nav: page indicator showing page 2 of 3 (My Wallet active). Main navigation: horizontal pager with 3 pages + page indicator. Design: bottom bar? The brief says \"Top level is a horizontal pager with 3 pages and a page indicator: page 1 (not part of this task), page 2 My Wallet, page 3 Discovery. The indicator must show the current page.\"\n\nHmm — \"Main navigation: page 2 of 3 (My Wallet)\". So the navigation is a pager — the page indicator must show current page. I'll design a bottom area with 3 dots + labels? Or a top segmented indicator? Let me do a bottom tab-like bar with three items: page 1 (unnamed — maybe \"Home\"?), My Wallet, Discovery. But page 1 is \"not part of this task\" — no frame for it. I could label it generically. Hmm, what would page 1 be? Not specified. Safer: