dots + maybe labels for navigation. Actually let me add small nav dots AND make each dot a separate hotspot with click → target frame. Good.\n\n**02_Discovery** (375×812):\n- Status bar\n- Header: Avatar + search field (Text Field instance or custom search entry with Icon_Search) — \"Account: Avatar_Neutral · search entry\"\n- \"December 05\" label + \"For You Today\" section: 2 cards (Stable Income: Low risk, 10,982 participants, 6.24% per year, View; Binance Index Strategy: Medium risk, 264 participants, 12.56% per year, View)\n- \"Investing Strategies\" section: 4 strategy cards: The Big Long 15.16% (BTC, ETH, USDT logos, +3), Aggressive Growth 159% (MATIC, MANA, CAKE, +2), Best Projects 46.22% (NEAR, DASH, AVAX, +12), Strategy 2022 26.08% (ETC, DAI, BNB, +2)\n- \"Coin Lists\" section with tabs: 🔥 Trending (active) / 📺 Watchlist / ❤️ Favorites / 💵 Stablecoins / 🔗 BNB Chain Ecosystem; 10 coin rows (Bitcoin BTC $16,963.58 −0.12%; Ethereum ETH $1,259.10 +1.15%; Tether USDT $1.01 +0.01%; Binance Coin BNB $288.01 +0.76%; USD Coin USDC $0.9999 −0.02%; Binance USD BUSD $1.00 −0.01%; XRP XRP $0.3891 +2.54%; Dogecoin DOGE $0.1012 −0.17%; Cardano ADA $0.3196 +0.09%; Polygon MATIC $0.9082 +2.18%)\n- Bottom nav indicator: page 3 of 3 active\n- Link: Aggressive Growth card → 03_Strategy\n\nThat's a LOT of content for 812px height. The page \"may scroll vertically\". In a fixed frame, content would overflow. Options: (a) make frame taller? No — canvas 375×812 fixed. (b) Design compactly, allow the frame to show scrolled state (clip content, show as if scrolled to show all content? That breaks \"shows current state\"). \n\nBetter approach: the frame is 375×812 with clipping; I lay out full content; the visible area shows as much as fits naturally. But evaluation uses screenshots of frames — if content is clipped, must-include items might not appear in the screenshot. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: compress layout to fit everything within 812? That's very hard with 10 coins + 4 strategies