{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete an unattended Figma product-design benchmark in the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/AkAgp4U0sCY7xkZ05uhVkb/ (fileKey `AkAgp4U0sCY7xkZ05uhVkb`). Requirements:\n   - Confirm account is zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai via whoami (done, confirmed).\n   - Read \"00 · Start Here\" for the brief; \"01 · Foundations\" for visual rules; reuse \"02 · Components\"; use \"04 · Media\" assets; deliver complete design into \"03 · Workspace\" (page 4:2, was empty).\n   - Preserve all reference pages; do not create a different file or switch accounts.\n   - Process: whoami → get_metadata → read-only inspection → use_figma to build → get_screenshot to verify; multiple fix/screenshot cycles allowed.\n   - Output requirement: before EVERY tool call and after every tool result include a visible \"Reasoning summary:\" prefixed line; final response starts with \"Reasoning summary: ...\" then \"Final answer:\" containing the assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, and remaining limitations.\n   - This is an unattended session: resolve routine choices using the brief; report real limitations if blocked.\n\n   The brief (from 00 · Start Here, frame 3:39): Design \"Investment Wallet — crypto wallet for beginners\". Build EXACTLY 5 frames named exactly `01_Wallet`, `02_Discovery`, `03_Strategy`, `04_Invest_Amount`, `05_Invest_Success`, one state per frame, wired as a clickable prototype. Canvas 375×812 iPhone, light mode. 01/02/03 may scroll vertically. Brand primary color #2B2D33 + Nunito are FIXED; every other color, type scale, spacing, radii, elevation are mine to define consistently. All business components must be reusable components. Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" verbatim. Brief wins over any known original kit.\n\n   Navigation structure: top level is a horizontal pager with 3 pages + page indicator (page 1 not in task; page 2 = My Wallet = 01_Wallet; page 3 = Discovery = 02_Discovery); indicator must show current page. 03/04/05 are sheets stacked over 02_Discovery (one frame each). Invest flow: 02→03→04→05. Entry-only (no frames/links needed): Send, Receive, scan, search, assets, pockets, Add Pocket, View on For You cards, other strategies, coins, non-Trending tabs, Max, swap currency.\n\n   Prototype links (required): 01_Wallet →(swipe/page indicator)→ 02_Discovery; 02_Discovery →(Aggressive Growth)→ 03_Strategy, →(swipe/page indicator)→ 01_Wallet; 03_Strategy →(Invest)→ 04_Invest_Amount, →(dismiss)→ 02_Discovery; 04_Invest_Amount →(back)→ 03_Strategy, →(Hold to Invest)→ 05_Invest_Success; 05_Invest_Success →(close)→ 02_Discovery, →(View Pocket)→ 01_Wallet.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via `use_figma` MCP tool (50k char limit per call, separate sandbox per call, no persistent helpers between calls)\n   - `figma.getNodeByIdAsync`, `figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` (must use, not currentPage setter), `loadFontAsync` before text ops\n   - ComponentNode.createInstance(), InstanceNode.swapComponent() for nested logo/icon swapping (test inconclusive), text/fill/size overrides on instance children\n   - Auto-layout frames (layoutMode, primaryAxisSizingMode/counterAxisSizingMode FIXED vs AUTO, SPACE_BETWEEN, padding, cornerRadius, individual strokeTopWeight)\n   - Media symbols are COMPONENT nodes: coin logos, Avatar_Neutral, icons — instantiate directly by ID\n   - Prototype reactions: `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'OnClick'|'OnDrag'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'DISSOLVE'|'MOVE_IN',...}}}]` — settabl