{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"03_Strategy looks quite good! Issues to fix:\n\n1. Fact chips: labels clipped badly — \"Mini mum invest ment\" wraps and gets cut (\"...ment\" partially cut at bottom), \"Recom mended invest...\" cut, \"Particip ants\" cut. The fact chips hug height now, but the label text at 9px in ~92px wraps to 3 lines and the chip height doesn't fully fit? Actually chips show text cut off at bottom — the chip instances hug height based on... hmm, the label has textAutoResize HEIGHT so it wraps, chip should grow. But the row frames (f1/f2) are horizontal AL hug — children should fit. Problem: instance height override? The chip master resize: `factC.resizeWithoutConstraints(108,factC.height)` — height at that moment was 46 fixed; setting counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO' before resize... The master height may still be pinned at 46 (primaryAxisSizingMode is height for horizontal AL — Chip/Fact is HORIZONTAL AL? Chip/Fact: children value + label — VERTICAL? I built Chip/Fact as... summary: \"Chip/Fact (108×46, bg #F5F6FA r12, children \"value\" 12 Bold + \"label\" 9 Medium)\". Layout direction unknown from summary — probably VERTICAL (value above label). If VERTICAL: primary=vertical (height), counter=horizontal (width 108). To hug height: primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' — but I set counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO' which made WIDTH hug! And then resizeWithoutConstraints(108,46) pinned width 108? Confusing. Metadata earlier: Chip/Fact 108×46.\n\n   In screenshot chips are ~108 wide and labels wrap+clip → height is FIXED at 46 (3 lines of 9px = 33 + value 15 + gap + pad 16 = 70 needed). Fix properly: inspect 5:12 layout: set primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' (if vertical) so height hugs, keep width fixed 108.\n\n2. Row 2 facts misaligned: \"🗓️ 2 Years / Recommended investment period\" chip shows \"Recom mended invest ment\" cut — same fix.\n\n3. Fact value emojis: 🌱 shows, 🔥 shows, 💵 shows, 🗓️ shows orange box, 🧑 shows. OK.\n\n4.