{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete an unattended Figma product-design benchmark in the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/AkAgp4U0sCY7xkZ05uhVkb/ (fileKey `AkAgp4U0sCY7xkZ05uhVkb`). Requirements:\n   - Confirm account is zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai via whoami (DONE in earlier session — confirmed).\n   - Read \"00 · Start Here\" for the brief; \"01 · Foundations\" for visual rules; reuse \"02 · Components\"; use \"04 · Media\" assets; deliver complete design into \"03 · Workspace\" (page `4:2`, was empty).\n   - Preserve all reference pages and their existing nodes; do not create a different file or switch accounts.\n   - Process: whoami → get_metadata → read-only inspection → use_figma to build → get_screenshot to verify; multiple fix/screenshot cycles allowed.\n   - OUTPUT PROTOCOL (critical): before EVERY tool call and after every tool result include a visible line prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:`; final response starts with `Reasoning summary: ...` then `Final answer:` containing the assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, and any remaining limitations. Never claim completion for unfinished work.\n   - Unattended session: resolve routine choices using the brief; report real limitations if blocked.\n\n   The brief (from 00 · Start Here, frame 3:39): Design \"Investment Wallet — crypto wallet for beginners\". Build EXACTLY 5 frames named exactly `01_Wallet`, `02_Discovery`, `03_Strategy`, `04_Invest_Amount`, `05_Invest_Success`, one state per frame, wired as a clickable prototype. Canvas 375×812 iPhone, light mode. 01/02/03 may scroll vertically. Brand primary #2B2D33 + Nunito are FIXED; every other color/type scale/spacing/radii/elevation are mine to define consistently. All business components must be reusable components. Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" verbatim (note U+2212 \"−\" for losses, curly quotes “ ” and ’).\n\n   Navigation: top level is a horizontal pager with 3 pages + indicator (page 1 not in task; page 2 = My Wallet = 01_Wallet; page 3 = Discovery = 02_Discovery); indicator must show current page. 03/04/05 are sheets stacked over 02_Discovery. Entry-only (no frames/links needed): Send, Receive, scan, search, assets, pockets, Add Pocket, View on For You cards, other strategies, coins, non-Trending tabs, Max, swap currency.\n\n   Required prototype links: 01_Wallet →(swipe/page indicator)→ 02_Discovery; 02_Discovery →(Aggressive Growth card)→ 03_Strategy, →(swipe/page indicator)→ 01_Wallet; 03_Strategy →(Invest)→ 04_Invest_Amount, →(dismiss)→ 02_Discovery; 04_Invest_Amount →(back)→ 03_Strategy, →(Hold to Invest)→ 05_Invest_Success; 05_Invest_Success →(close)→ 02_Discovery, →(View Pocket)→ 01_Wallet.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via `use_figma` MCP tool (50k char limit/call; separate sandbox per call)\n   - CRITICAL: `console.log` output is NOT returned; but RETURN VALUES ARE — end scripts with `return JSON.stringify({...})` from the async IIFE to surface results\n   - `InstanceNode.swapComponent()` EXISTS and works in this environment, but `instance.componentId` property does NOT exist (throws) — avoid reading it; factory-per-data-variant approach used instead (each Row/Coin · X, Card/Strategy · X etc. is its own component with baked data, so frames just place instances with zero overrides)\n   - Icon recoloring must set BOTH `fills` AND `strokes` on all descendants (Icon_Send is stroke-based; fills-only recolor left it invisible on dark). Pattern: `recolorAll(node,hex)` iterating `findAll(nn=>'fills' in nn)` and `findAll(nn=>'strokes' in nn)` with try/catch\n   - VERTICAL auto-layout: height = primaryAxisSizingMode, width = counterAxisSizingMode (Pager fix: counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' then resizeWithoutConstraints(375,h)); HORIZONTAL is the reverse\n   - Wrapping text in auto-layout: `textAutoResize='HEIGHT'` + `layoutAlign='STRETCH'`\n   - Instance child overrides allowed: text characters/fills, fills on instance root, position (x/y), resize — used heavily\n   - Prototype reactions to be set as `node.reactions=[{trigger:{type:'OnClick'|'OnDrag'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{...}}}]`; try direct on instance children, fallback invisible hotspot rects (opacity ~0.001)\n   - Transitions: try `{type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:250}` for sheets, catch → `{type:'DISSOLVE', duration:250}`\n   - Nunito styles loaded: \"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\",\"ExtraBold\"\n   - get_screenshot with `enableBase64Response:true` returns inline images (the only way to view them here)\n   - `figma.getNodeByIdAsync` with a wrong ID returns null (then `.findOne` on null throws and aborts the whole try block — verify IDs before chaining)\n   - Emoji render muted/gray for some glyphs in tab chips (📺💵🔗) — acceptable, not fixable\n   - Clone-before-reactions rule: background clones were made BEFORE any reactions exist, so no interaction leakage\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma file AkAgp4U0sCY7xkZ05uhVkb pages: `0:1` (00·Start Here), `1:2` (01·Foundations), `1:3` (02·Components), `1:4` (04·Media), `4:2` (03·Workspace — delivery target, all work is here).\n   - Given components: Button `3:19` (335×52 dark pill, text child \"Invest\" id 3:20), Text Field `3:22` (335×48), Status Bar `3:26` (375×44), Home Indicator `3:36` (375×34).\n   - Media component IDs: Coin_BTC `2:8`, ETH `2:11`, USDT `2:14`, BNB `2:17`, USDC `2:20`, BUSD `2:23`, XRP `2:26`, DOGE `2:29`, ADA `2:32`, MATIC `2:35`, DAI `2:38`, AVAX `2:41`, CAKE `2:44`, MANA `2:47`, MKR `2:50`, NEAR `2:53`,