{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reasoning summary: Sheet/Success built (12:917, h=335, instance at y=477 in 05). Body copy verified verbatim with curly quotes. Now S8: wire all prototype reactions.\n\nReactions plan:\n1. 01_Wallet (7:52): pager instance 9:129 → OnDrag → 9:137 (02_Discovery). Also dot3 click.\n2. 02_Discovery (9:137): st2 instance 9:191 (Aggressive Growth card) → OnClick → 10:267. Pager 9:303 → OnDrag → 7:52.\n3. 03_Strategy (10:267): sheet instance → find 'invest' button child → OnClick → 10:299; header 'back' icon → 9:137; 'close' icon → 9:137.\n4. 04_Invest_Amount (10:299): sheet 'back' → 10:267; 'hold' → 10:331.\n5. 05_Invest_Success (10:331): 'close' → 9:137; 'viewPocket' → 7:52.\n\nReactions on instance children: set node.reactions on the instance child directly. In Figma plugin API, you CAN set reactions on children of instances if they're interactive (it works for overrides). Let me try with try/catch; fallback to invisible hotspot rects in the frame.\n\nTransition: for sheets, try {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:250} — actually for overlays it'd be smart animate or move in. If throws, fallback DISSOLVE. For OnDrag trigger — reactions trigger type 'OnDrag'.\n\nLet me write the script with a helper:\n\nasync function link(srcNode, destId, trigger, transition) {\n  try {\n    srcNode.reactions = [{trigger: trigger, action: {type:'NODE', destinationId: destId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition}}];\n    return true;\n  } catch(e) { return false; }\n}\n\nFor finding children within instances: sheetInst.findOne(n=>n.name==='invest'). Within instance, children are editable.\n\nNote: OnDrag on the whole pager instance (9:129) — drag on pager area. Good.\n\nAlso dot clicks: dots are tiny; skip? Brief says \"swipe/page indicator\". The pager dots clicking — I planned dot3/dot2 clicks as backup. Dots inside instances — try setting reactions on them too, wrapped in try/catch.\n\nTransition types: 'MOVE_IN' with direction 'BOTTOM' — valid Plugin API TransitionType: {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM'} plus duration/easing. Let me use {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:250, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}. If it throws, use {type:'DISSOLVE', duration:250}.\n\nActually for 01→02 pager swipe, MOVE_IN direction 'LEFT' or 'RIGHT'? The pager is horizontal: from My Wallet (page 2) to Discovery (page 3) swipes left (content moves left, new page comes from right). Navigation 'NAVIGATE' with transition MOVE_IN direction 'LEFT' means destination moves in from the right. That's right for 01→02. For 02→01: MOVE_IN direction 'RIGHT'.\n\nFor sheets coming up from bottom: MOVE_IN direction 'BOTTOM' means destination slides in from bottom. For dismiss (03→02): MOVE_IN direction 'BOTTOM' as well (sheet slides down, revealing... actually dismiss would be MOVE_OUT but NAVIGATE only supports MOVE_IN from a direction — the reverse direction would be ideal but we can just use MOVE_IN BOTTOM; it looks like sheet sliding up which isn't a true dismiss, but acceptable). Hmm, for dismiss maybe DISSOLVE is cleaner. I'll use MOVE_IN BOTTOM for open (03→04 etc.) and DISSOLVE for dismiss actions. Keep it simple and robust.\n\nScript S8. Find nodes:\n- pager1 = 9:129 (instance in 01) → dest 9:137, trigger OnDrag, transition MOVE_IN LEFT.\n- dots in 9:129: dot3 child — find by name 'dot3' → OnClick → 9:137.\n- pager2 = 9:303 (in 02) → dest 7:52, OnDrag MOVE_IN RIGHT; dot2 → OnClick → 7:52.\n- st2 = 9:191 → OnClick → 10:267, DISSOLVE or MOVE_IN BOTTOM? It's a sheet over Discovery — MOVE_IN BOTTOM fits.\n- In 10:267: sheet instance — find by name 'sheet' → findOne 'invest' → OnClick → 10:299 MOVE_IN BOTTOM. Header back/close icons: header is a Header/Sheet instance inside sheet instance; find by names 'back'/'close' → OnClick → 9:137 DISSOLVE.\n- In 10:299: sheet → 'back' → 10:267 DISSOLVE; 'hold' → 10:331 MOVE_IN BOTTOM.\n- In 10:331: sheet → 'close' → 9:137 DISSOLVE; 'viewPocket' → 7:52 DISSOLVE.\n\nCareful: header instances inside sheet instances — Header/Sheet master has children named 'back', 'title', 'close'. findOne on the sheet instance will find them.\n\nSet reactions on instance children directly. If that throws (not allowed on instance sublayers?), fallback: create hotspot rect in the FRAME (not instance) positioned over the child's absolute position. Let me include fallback: after attempting, check result; if false, create hotspot. For simplicity, collect failures and then create hotspots for failed ones with absolute bounding box positions.\n\nHotspot creation: figma.createRectangle? Better: figma.createRectangle with fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:{r:0,g:0,b:0},opacity:0.001}] and reactions set. Position: use absoluteBoundingBox of target minus frame absolute position. Frame at x=0 on page? Frames are at x=0,475,950,1425,1900. abs coords computed.\n\nLet me write it. For destinationId in reactions: must be node ID string — fine.\n\nOne concern: setting `reactions` on a child INSIDE an instance — Figma supports \"interactions on nested instances\" since overrides... Actually the Plugin API allows setting reactions on any node, including instance children, as long as the node is not locked... I believe it works. Try/catch + fallback anyway.\n\nReturn JSON with per-link results.","signature":"9963fe291ae448efa08f4d63"}],"id":"e8be0706-2598-40e3-8aa8-44dcd49e442a","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b54d81e-1062-44f7-87fa-749cc21f1674","uuid":"d369ed5e-ac9e-4621-aa34-63a92f37dafb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:07:40.255Z","thinking_duration_ms":27797}
