{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reasoning summary: The error message reveals the exact schema. Key findings:\n- Trigger: `ON_CLICK` / `ON_DRAG` (SCREAMING_SNAKE), not 'OnClick'/'OnDrag'.\n- Action type 'NODE' IS valid — but the error at the bottom of the validation (in `navaction` try, which passed type:'NAVIGATE') shows the accepted NODE shape: `{type:'NODE', navigation:..., transition:...}` with:\n  - `navigation` required ('NAVIGATE' presumably)\n  - `transition` required with **`easing` REQUIRED**, and transition.type must be 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT' — DISSOLVE is invalid in this API version.\n\nSo correct format:\n```js\n{\n  trigger: {type:'ON_CLICK'},\n  action: {\n    type:'NODE',\n    destinationId:'7:52',\n    navigation:'NAVIGATE',\n    transition:{type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:250, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}\n  }\n}\n```\nWait — does NODE action accept destinationId? In the minimal try, error said \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" for NODE type — that's because... hmm, look closer: for `type:'NODE'` the error says \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\"... That's confusing — it seems the validator tried matching the object against several schemas and NODE with navigation='NAVIGATE'... wait no.\n\nActually in the first try, action = {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition}. The validator matched against multiple union branches:\n1. CONDITIONAL — no\n2. {type:'BACK'|'CLOSE'} — received 'NODE' → no\n3. {type:'URL', url} — no\n4. UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME — no\n5. {type:'NAVIGATE'?...} — hmm, one branch says \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following... Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing ... Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN'|'MOVE_OUT'|'PUSH'|'SLIDE_IN'|'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE'\" — that branch accepted type/navigation but rejected the transition shape (missing easing, DISSOLVE invalid).\n6. SET_VARIABLE — no.\n\nSo the NODE branch exists (branch 5 shows transition validation happening while destinationId/navigation were accepted). The only problems: DISSOLVE invalid and easing missing.\n\nIn the third try (navaction with type:'NAVIGATE'), the last branch listed: \"Invalid literal value, expected 'NODE' at [0].action.type; Required value missing at [0].action.navigation; Expected transition to be one of the following... (same transition complaints)\". So NODE action requires: navigation (='NAVIGATE'), transition with valid type + easing.\n\nEasing format: {type:'EASE_OUT'} — Plugin API easing: Easing object like {type:'EASE_OUT'} or {type:'CUSTOM_CUBIC_BEZIER', ...}. Should be fine.\n\nAlso for DISSOLVE alternative — not available; use MOVE_IN/SLIDE_IN. For simple fades there's no dissolve, but SMART_ANIMATE? The enum listed: 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT'. Hmm, SMART_ANIMATE not listed in error but error may just list the ones relevant. I'll use:\n- Sheets open: {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:250, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}\n- Dismiss: {type:'SLIDE_OUT'...}? SLIDE_OUT with direction BOTTOM would slide the current screen out revealing... in NAVIGATE context the destination comes in. For dismiss 03→02, I could use MOVE_OUT? Actually for NAVIGATE, destination is the new screen. The transition describes how the new screen arrives. For a dismiss feel: SLIDE_IN from... none feel like dismiss. Simplest: use MOVE_IN BOTTOM for open (sheet slides up — good), and for dismiss use MOVE_OUT? Not sure MOVE_OUT applies to destination. Keep it simple: dismiss = {type:'DISSOLVE'} invalid → use {type:'SLIDE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM'}? That's same as MOVE_IN roughly. Honestly the cleanest \"back\" feel: destination slides in from bottom (as if sheet slides down revealing the screen beneath — visually the discovery screen appears from bottom). That's acceptable. Or PUSH LEFT for pager.\n\nPager: 01→02 {type:'SLIDE_IN', direction:'LEFT'}? For horizontal pager, new page comes from right: direction 'LEFT' means slides leftward into place (from right side). I'll use SLIDE_IN LEFT for 01→02 and SLIDE_IN RIGHT for 02→01. Actually MOVE_IN vs SLIDE_IN: SLIDE_IN slides destination over; PUSH pushes current out. For pager, PUSH LEFT is most pager-like. I'll use PUSH LEFT/RIGHT for pager, MOVE_IN BOTTOM for sheets, and for dismiss MOVE_IN BOTTOM too (sheet slides down = destination appears... eh). Fine — duration 250.\n\nAlso need duration + easing in transition. Let me redo S8 with corrected schema. Also note `reactions` setter on instance children failed earlier due to validation, not permission — so it may work now with correct format.\n\nTransition schema guess: {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:250, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}. Some versions require easing as EasingFunction object. {type:'EASE_OUT'} is valid Easing.\n\nRewrite S8 with corrected links. Keep hotspot fallback but it likely won't be needed now. Also, IMPORTANT: the failed S8 attempt may have left some hotspots? No — in failed run, ensureHotspot created rects only when first link failed... wait, look at the code: `if(!res.p1drag){await ensureHotspot(...)}` — p1drag was false, so ensureHotspot ran and created a rect, then link failed again and pushed to failures — but the rect was NOT removed! So there are 12 orphan hotspot rects (opacity 0.001, named hotspot_*) sitting on frames 7:52, 9:137 (several), 10:267, 10:299, 10:331. I must delete them: findAll on each frame for name starting with 'hotspot_' and remove. Do that in the new script before wiring.","signature":"e11ad64935be42bc80cc78b4"}],"id":"96f17ad0-a7ee-40e9-b53b-a4d194d1fe71","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b54d81e-1062-44f7-87fa-74