{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reasoning summary: All variants fail, even `{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE'}` with no transition — and the error says for NODE branch: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\". This strongly suggests that in THIS API version, the NODE action schema doesn't accept type:'NODE' — it expects action types 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' for the navigation family, or maybe the navigation-to-node is expressed differently. The earlier full error had a branch: \"Invalid literal value, expected 'NODE' at [0].action.type; Required value missing at [0].action.navigation\" — that appeared in the navaction probe (action.type='NAVIGATE'). So there IS a branch with literal 'NODE' and required `navigation`... but when we send type:'NODE' it says \"Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\"?? That's contradictory — unless there are TWO different branches and the one with literal 'NODE' requires `navigation` PLUS transition with easing, and the \"Expected 'BACK'|'CLOSE'\" message is from a DIFFERENT branch that's listed first.\n\nWait, actually re-reading probe 1 minimal try with full error: branches listed in order:\n1. CONDITIONAL\n2. \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\" — branch: {type:'BACK'|'CLOSE'}\n3. URL\n4. UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME (x3 variants)\n5. \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following...\" — this branch validated transition (so type+navigation were ACCEPTED here), failing on transition shape only.\n6. SET_VARIABLE\n7. SET_VARIABLE_MODE\n\nSo branch 5 = {type:'NODE', navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{...}} — type:'NODE' accepted there! The failure was ONLY in transition: \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" and \"Invalid enum value ... received 'DISSOLVE'\". So with easing + valid type it should pass...\n\nBut probe with easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'} still failed. Why? Maybe easing format is different: Easing in this API version might be {type:'EASE_OUT'} per docs... OR the transition requires `matchLayers` key? Error mentioned \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.matchLayers\" in the DISSOLVE attempt — that was part of a sub-branch for smart-animate-ish transitions. Let me look at that transition sub-validation more carefully from probe 1:\n\n\"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched:\n  Expected ...:\n    Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\n    Multiple issues at [0].action.transition:\n      Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE' at [0].action.transition.type\n      Required value missing at [0].action.transition.direction\n      Required value missing at [0].action.transition.matchLayers\n      Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\n  Expected null, received object at [0].action.transition\"\n\nSo transition union has TWO branches:\na) {type:'INSTANT'|'DISSOLVE'?? no...} requiring ONLY easing (with type accepted? since it says required easing missing and nothing else) — branch a = {type: <some literal that matched>, easing: required}. Since only \"Required value missing at easing\" was reported, our type 'DISSOLVE' was accepted by branch a?? But then it complained about easing missing. So branch a might be {type:'INSTANT'|'DISSOLVE', easing}. Hmm but it received 'DISSOLVE' and the enum complaint was only in branch b. So branch a accepts DISSOLVE and requires easing!\nb) directional branch: requires type in MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT/PUSH/SLIDE_IN/SLIDE_OUT + direction + matchLayers?? + easing. Wait \"Required value missing at matchLayers\" — hmm, matchLayers required? That seems like the SMART_ANIMATE branch. Actually for MOVE_IN etc., matchLayers isn't normally required. But the error lists it as required in that branch. Odd but let's just satisfy it: include matchLayers: null? Hmm.\n\nAlso there's \"Expected null, received object at [0].action.transition\" — a branch where transition must be null?? That's the instant/no-transition branch.\n\nSo possible winning transition candidates:\n- {type:'DISSOLVE', easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}} — branch a (maybe duration optional)\n- {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}, matchLayers:null} — branch b with all required keys\n- add duration too (250). Duration might be required? Not listed as missing — in branch b the missing keys were direction, matchLayers, easing (when type was invalid everything else is also flagged...). Zod reports all issues at once usually. In branch b with type='DISSOLVE' invalid, it reported the enum error AND missing direction, matchLayers, easing — but NOT missing duration. So duration optional or required-not-reported? Zod would report required missing duration too. So duration is optional.\n\nPlan: try a matrix on probe rect:\n1. {type:'DISSOLVE', easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}, duration:250}\n2. {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}, duration:250, matchLayers:null}\n3. {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}, duration:250} (no matchLayers)\n4. {type:'PUSH', direction:'LEFT', easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}, duration:250, matchLayers:null}\n5. easing as {type:'EASE_OUT'} vs maybe needs 'EASE_OUT' string? Try easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'} first.\n\nAlso full error for the winning/losing to see. Truncate less (1500 chars) and return each error fully for the first two.","signature":"ad767f2f13f24ebc82a671c6"}],"id":"0442c3f4-9e71-48fd-aa66-734583b7f701","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b54d81e-1062-44f7-87fa-749cc21f1674","uuid":"a03c5a23-1d70-4368-ad09-83b22068a5c0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:10:37.212Z","thinking_duration_ms":25569}
