lures in the rerun truncated at 100 chars so I couldn't see if it was schema or semantic.\n\nHypothesis: transition branch structure: branch a = {type:'DISSOLVE'|'INSTANT', easing, duration?} — accepts DISSOLVE. Branch b = directional (MOVE_IN etc.) requires direction, matchLayers, easing? Earlier probe \"mv-matchNull\" with matchLayers:null + easing failed. Maybe matchLayers must be an ARRAY or true? For MOVE_IN, Figma's Transition includes matchLayers?: boolean... Actually Figma's Transition union: SimpleTransition ({type:'DISSOLVE'|'INSTANT'|'SMART_ANIMATE', duration, easing}) and DirectionalTransition ({type:'MOVE_IN'|'MOVE_OUT'|'PUSH'|'SLIDE_IN'|'SLIDE_OUT', duration, easing, direction, matchLayers?}). matchLayers should be optional boolean. Hmm but error earlier said required.\n\nWait — maybe the issue in mv probes was easing! Maybe easing must be {type:'EASE_OUT'} — I used that. Hmm, or maybe easing type enum differs: 'EASE_OUT' vs 'EASE_OUT' should be fine per Figma docs (Easing = {type:'EASE_IN'|'EASE_OUT'|'EASE_IN_OUT'|'LINEAR'|'CUSTOM_CUBIC_BEZIER'...}).\n\nLet me probe systematically inside a REAL frame context: put probe rect INSIDE frame 10:267 (as a valid prototype source), and test:\n1. DISSOLVE+easing → dest 7:52 (semantic should pass: different top-level frame, same page)\n2. MOVE_IN BOTTOM + easing (no matchLayers)\n3. MOVE_IN BOTTOM + easing + matchLayers:true\n4. PUSH LEFT + easing\n5. SLIDE_IN BOTTOM + easing\n\nEach: try, record ok or first 300 chars of error. Then remove probe.","signature":"6c033a7f3a6f4b4babf2f5aa"}],"id":"e03b8abb-b88f-41cb-8be5-a5fa4034d6b5","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b54d81e-1062-44f7-87fa-749cc21f1674","uuid":"1c5a07b8-26cb-4947-a241-602f6b7f8a79","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:12:08.973Z","thinking_duration_ms":18059}
